{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"color","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLWedgeV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/color"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge":{"title":"MXLWedge","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge","abstract":[{"text":"The wedge type represents crescendo and diminuendo wedge symbols. The type attribute is crescendo for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a wedge that is closed at the left side, and diminuendo for the start of a wedge that is closed on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right side. Spread values are measured in tenths; those at the start of a crescendo wedge or end of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diminuendo wedge are ignored. The niente attribute is yes if a circle appears at the point of the wedge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating a crescendo from nothing or diminuendo to nothing. It is no by default, and used only when the type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is crescendo, or the type is stop for a wedge that began with a diminuendo type. The line-type is solid if not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge/color":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"color","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/color","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}